# Writing rules

- First person, plain voice. Short sentences.
- No em dashes or en dashes anywhere in copy. Use commas, periods, or colons.
- Say what the thing does before saying what it is built with.
- Never write a number that is not in `portfolio-facts`. No invented percentages, user
  counts, latencies, or team sizes.

## Banned filler

Never use: leveraging, passionate about, cutting-edge, seamless, journey, crafting
experiences. Same goes for their close cousins (empowering, robust suite, game-changing).

## Examples

```
// BAD
Passionate about leveraging cutting-edge GenAI to craft seamless geospatial experiences,
delivering a 40% improvement in pipeline throughput.

// GOOD
I owned the data pipeline behind a live consumer site. Python and DuckDB, served from
Cloudflare R2.
```

```
// BAD (em dash, stack before substance)
A Next.js and DuckDB pipeline — rescuing federal infrastructure data.

// GOOD
Republished 400+ DHS infrastructure and resilience layers so they stay public. Built with
GDAL, GeoParquet, and PMTiles.
```
